+Whether it does is an empirical question, and it has not been answered against a certified survey. The evaluations published so far compare LLM agents with rule-based agents on scenario plausibility, or on aggregate patterns of their own making. None measures the distance between the modal split produced by a population of LLM agents and the modal split observed on the same territory, under a protocol that gives tabular models the same information. This paper addresses this question.
 
